@title Yggdra Union - We'll Never Fight Alone (USA)
@file Yggdra Union - We'll Never Fight Alone (U).gba
@game BYUE
@chip EEPROM 64Kbit
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# Health warning, START through the intro twice, title > NEW GAME,
# tutorials Yes, the prologue, Chapter 1, A through the thieves' talk, CARD
# SELECT: all five cards (Steal, Mind Change, Refresh, Mirage, Rockfall),
# START > character, START > "Ready for combat?" A, the Tutorial Corner
# (taps every 110 frames: its text types slowly), Milanor two steps down
# next to the thieves, A, the attack tutorial, START (Union) > RIGHT onto
# the Assassin > A > "Union Formed! Ready for combat?" A: the battle (You
# Win, 5 to 0), the end-turn tutorial, L > Main Menu > Suspend > OK: the
# suspend save (8 KB of EEPROM). [load]: title > CONTINUE > OK resumes the
# map at the Main Menu (the game erases the suspend save once it is loaded,
# in every emulator), B closes it.
# The battle animates ahead on mgba (union_formed, you_win; dingbat = the second reference).
# suspend_prompt reads SLIP(-1) against both references, which agree only by
# coincidence: frame by frame from the L menu (f41490-41600) the second reference runs the
# menu, its fade and the prompt one frame after dingbat with dingbat's
# pictures, while mgba keeps dingbat's frames but its own pictures (another
# phase of the prompt's 2-frame blink, which lands on the second reference's). The save's
# progress bar fills on a timer, the same in all three (the second reference a frame late).
# The "SUCCEEDED" screen walks two small unit icons whose pose follows those
# phases, so saved is judged by its text. The three battery files differ in six bytes
# (and the checksum); no byte has dingbat alone against the two references
# (the second reference stands alone at 0x97, 0x25D, 0x2A5 and 0x2BD, mgba at 0x10B, all three
# differ at 0x275), and every emulator loads every save to the same screens.

